       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release tablets, so this is twice that limit. Metformin at this dose raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThese are some options within the label:\n- **Metformin IR 850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the labeled maximum.\n- **Metformin IR 500 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is a common starting dose, and you can titrate up.\n- **Metformin IR 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals.** This is 2,000 mg/day.\n\nWas 1700 mg meant to be the total daily dose, for example 850 mg twice daily? Or was it a typo? If you give me the intended dose, I'll enter it right away."
